# Changelog — 2026-03-07 12:38.1

## Ad hoc: Remove cmd.exe, fix WSL detection, align path selector

### Problem
- Git Bash path selector was indented 40px from radio buttons instead of left-aligned
- WSL detection used `existsSync('wsl.exe')` which returns true on all modern Windows
  (wsl.exe is pre-installed) even when no WSL distributions are installed
- cmd.exe shell option doesn't work properly with our xterm.js/node-pty terminal
  (archaic, non-standard terminal semantics)

### What Changed

#### Path Selector Alignment (`SettingsTab.ts`)
- Removed `marginLeft: '40px'` from both `createPathSelector` and `createPathInput`
- Path input now left-aligns with radio buttons

#### WSL Detection (`main.ts`)
- `check-wsl-available` IPC handler now runs `wsl.exe --list --quiet` and checks
  for installed distributions instead of just checking if `wsl.exe` exists
- Uses `execFileSync` with utf16le encoding (WSL outputs UTF-16), 5s timeout
- Returns `false` if no distros are installed or if the command fails

#### cmd.exe Removed
- Removed `'cmd'` from `ShellType` union in both `SettingsTab.ts` and `terminal-service.ts`
- Removed cmd.exe from shell options UI (was "Command Prompt")
- Removed cmd case from `resolveShellPath()` and `getShellArgs()`
- Git Bash fallback now goes to PowerShell instead of cmd.exe
- Shell options: Git Bash, PowerShell, WSL Bash (Windows) / Linux Shell (Linux)

### Files Changed
- `src/renderer/components/SettingsTab.ts` — path alignment, remove cmd option
- `src/main/services/terminal-service.ts` — remove cmd from ShellType and switch cases
- `src/main/main.ts` — WSL detection via `wsl --list --quiet`
- `src/tests/core-0.8.0/terminal-shell.test.ts` — update type test
- `src/tests/core-0.8.0/settings-tab.test.ts` — remove Command Prompt assertion
- `src/tests/core-0.4.0/terminal-service.test.ts` — fallback now PowerShell

